10. Future Mechanical Expansion

After validating the initial six-dot cell, the design may be expanded to four cells, producing a total of 24 tactile dots.

Expansion will require additional mechanical modules, coordinated actuator control, suitable packaging and validation of the complete display.

The four-cell configuration remains a stretch goal. The first priority is a mechanically reliable and independently controllable six-dot cell.

11. Current Status

The mechanical architecture and design priorities have been documented. The final pin guide, servo linkages, dimensions, CAD assembly and manufacturing process still need to be developed and validated.

The next steps are to create the CAD model, confirm that the selected servos can produce the required pin movement, manufacture the initial components and evaluate the assembled mechanism.

No mechanical performance claims are considered verified until supported by physical testing.

